1
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Every order in this city starts with a human body on two wheels.

2
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Every plane has a black box. Every car. The worker has nothing.

3
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
No employer. No insurance. No proof. Just an algorithm with a countdown.

4
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Hong Kong just said: platforms will pay.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
You cannot pay for a crash nobody can prove.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
One in three riders runs two apps at once. Two companies. One body. Who pays?

7
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
A law without evidence is a promise without a price.

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
So we built the black box for the human body.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
A 3D-printed clip and a forty-dollar board. On the helmet they already wear. Talks to the phone they already carry.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Impact. Fall. Stillness. Three signals. Few things look like that.

11
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Thirty seconds to say "I'm fine". Silence, and triage knows where and how hard.

12
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
No new hardware needed to start. The phone in your pocket is already the sensor.

13
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Same second, the insurance fires. No form. No adjuster. Paid in a day.

14
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,000
It knows which app the rider was on at the moment of impact.

15
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,000
"Which company pays" becomes a lookup. Not a lawsuit.

16
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Heat and fatigue warnings go to the rider. Never the boss.

17
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,000
The rider owns the data. Everyone else sees events. Never a route. Never a score.

18
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
We are not an insurer. We are the evidence.

19
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Hong Kong writes the law. We write the standard. Next door, 84 million workers are waiting for one.

20
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Same rider. Same crash. Two different worlds.

21
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Same rider. Same rain. Same order.

22
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Impact. Fall. Stillness. The model sees it in under a second. The old rule would have missed it.

23
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:10,000
No answer. Triage already knows where, and how hard.

24
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,000
One event. One payout. No argument.

25
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Which app. Which order. Which second. Done.

26
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
That is what one typhoon cost one rider.

27
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Insurers get a loss history. Platforms get a fair premium. Riders get paid.

28
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Four disciplines. One problem.

29
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
We built it, then broke it until it told the truth.

30
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
It answers to the rider first.

31
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,000
And it pays.

32
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Metrics. Proof for the people who keep this city moving.
